@startuml git-branches-and-blame-component
title E2 — Component Overview

package "ide-core" {
  [GitRepo] as GitRepo
  [git2 (libgit2)] as Git2
}

package "ide-ui" {
  [IdeApp] as IdeApp
  [GitPanel] as GitPanel
  [editor::blame_gutter\n(pure logic)] as BlameGutter
  [editor::geometry] as Geometry
  [EditorTab] as EditorTab
}

database "Working tree\n(.git + files on disk)" as Disk

IdeApp --> GitPanel : branch-widget click\nopens branches popup
GitPanel --> GitRepo : branches() / create_branch()\nswitch_branch() / delete_branch()\nmerge_branch() / commit()
IdeApp --> EditorTab : toggle blame\n(gutter context menu\n/ command palette)
EditorTab --> GitRepo : blame_file(path)
EditorTab --> BlameGutter : annotations_from_blame()
BlameGutter --> Geometry : reserved lane width\n(toggle-scoped, not\nper-frame recomputed)
IdeApp --> GitRepo : commit_detail(id)\n(blame popup)
GitRepo --> Git2 : wraps
Git2 --> Disk : read history/blame,\nwrite branch refs,\ncheckout working tree,\nwrite merge commit

note right of GitRepo
  Local-only: no fetch/pull/push,
  no remote-tracking info. Same
  "no subprocess, no network I/O"
  guarantee as git-support-component.
end note

@enduml
